  "id": "COMPOUND:43464 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "Alloocimene, (4Z,6Z)- is linked to CCF-STTG1 through a series of molecular interactions that involve carboxylesterase 2 and other compounds. The evidence suggests that Alloocimene acts as a target for carboxylesterase 2, which in turn targets (7E,9E,16Z)-18-hydroxyoctadeca-7,9,16-trien-11,13-diyn-4-one, a compound that ultimately has a target of CCF-STTG1. Additionally, Alloocimene is linked to hepatocytes, which are targeted by S-ethylcysteine zwitterion, a compound that also targets CCF-STTG1. These pathways highlight a complex network of molecular interactions, where Alloocimene may influence CCF-STTG1 through indirect mechanisms involving enzyme activity and compound targeting. The evidence supports a potential role for Alloocimene in modulating CCF-STTG1 through a series of enzymatic and molecular interactions, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
